cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the papers it follows."
title: "Monty on the BEAM"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ledentsov
    given-names: Dmitry
    website: "https://github.com/d-led"
repository-code: "https://github.com/d-led/ex.tbp.monty"
license: MPL-2.0
version: "0.1.3"
abstract: >-
  The Thousand Brains Project's Monty rewritten in Elixir: a module-for-module
  port of the sensorimotor framework, from the sensor module and the learning
  modules to the experiment loop, with a studio for running Monty's experiments
  and an MCP interface to Monty's documentation.
keywords:
  - thousand brains
  - Monty
  - sensorimotor
  - object recognition
  - pose estimation
  - Elixir
# Zenodo mints a DOI for each GitHub release; add it as `doi:` once the first
# release has been archived.
